  dollName: Clawdia
  dollOwner: Payton High, 7 y.o., female, alive
  dollStory: "Payton bought Clawdia at a shopping mall with her mother. The doll
    has a sound effect that plays when it is pushed too hard. Therefore, during the
    physical discomfort test, ignore the doll\u2019s meowing. Payton\u2019s parents
    reported seeing the doll move rapidly around Payton\u2019s room \u2014 a behavior
    that is certainly not part of the doll\u2019s design. Although Clawdia has never
    harmed anyone, the parents remain concerned."
  dollReason: Clawdia harbors a spirit that appears to be playful, with no intention
    of causing harm. However, playful or not, spirits within these dolls are typically
    destroyed. Neutral dolls can be placed in either box if it is determined that
    the doll is truly safe to be returned to its owner.
